      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/laevimon-kottelati-2/",
      "html": "<p>Laevimon kottelati is a freshwater crab that reaches a size of about 4.5 cm carapace width. It is endemic to Vietnam.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/laevimon-kottelati-2/",
      "html": "<p>Endemic to Vietnam. It was discovered there in 1998 and scientifically described in 2005 as a new species in a new genus.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/laevimon-kottelati-2/",
      "html": "<p>It lives amphibiously in the shallow water of the banks of small rivers.</p>"
    },
